requests.description:
The assessor starts a visit to a SPECIFIC FIELD they are going to assess. Only `fieldId` is sent - the farmer and program are derived from the field on the server. Requires an ASSESSOR token.

Authorization: the assessor must be allowed to assess that field (it is enrolled in a program where they are the assigned assessor, and the program has started) - otherwise 403. Field must exist (else 404). One active visit per assessor (else 409). The destination pin is the field’s own coordinates.

On success the farmer gets a `visit:incoming` socket push AND a persistent notification naming the field ("... has started a visit to \"North Field\".").

### Expected (201)
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Visit started.",
  "data": { "visit": {
    "id": "...", "assessor_id": "...", "farmer_id": "...",
    "field_id": "...", "field_name": "North Field", "program_id": "...",
    "status": "en_route", "dest_latitude": 28.55, "dest_longitude": 77.33,
    "last_latitude": null, "last_longitude": null, "started_at": "..."
  } }
}
```
